WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.408
Here are 8 numbers.

00:02.408 --> 00:08.997
How many subarrays, runs of neighbours, add up to 7?

00:08.997 --> 00:14.700
Adding up every run one by one takes 36 sums.

00:15.000 --> 00:21.195
Instead, keep a running total, the prefix sum.

00:21.195 --> 00:31.700
Any run adds up to the total at its end minus the total just before it starts.

00:32.000 --> 00:41.196
So at each number, ask a hash map how many earlier totals equal the total minus 7.

00:41.196 --> 00:45.345
Each one starts a run that ends here.

00:45.345 --> 00:47.700
Then store the total.

00:48.000 --> 00:50.340
One pass finds all 4.

00:50.340 --> 00:53.906
That’s O(n) time and O(n) space.

00:53.906 --> 00:59.700
That’s prefix sum: keep running totals and subtract.
